Subject: clk: qcom: camcc-sc8280xp: give the eight GDSCs their reset wait values

The sc8280xp camcc driver leaves en_rest_wait_val / en_few_wait_val /
clk_dis_wait_val unset, so gdsc_init() overwrites the hardware reset values
with gdsc.c's MSM8974-era defaults. Read back on this board: GDSCR =
0x00282801, i.e. 2 / 8 / 2. Every same-generation camcc driver with the same
register offsets (camcc-sm8150, camcc-sc8180x, and the sc7280, sm6350,
sm8550, sm8650, sa8775p and x1e80100 ones) writes 2 / 2 / 0xf. This restores
those values. It is part of the gaokun3 camera power-domain fix and is
written for upstream alongside the RCG change in the next patch.
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sc8280xp.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sc8280xp.c
index 660d865..e4ec7e3 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sc8280xp.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sc8280xp.c
@@ -2711,6 +2711,9 @@ static struct gdsc titan_top_gdsc;
 
 static struct gdsc bps_gdsc = {
 	.gdscr = 0x7004,
+	.en_rest_wait_val = 0x2,
+	.en_few_wait_val = 0x2,
+	.clk_dis_wait_val = 0xf,
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "bps_gdsc",
 	},
@@ -2721,6 +2724,9 @@ static struct gdsc bps_gdsc = {
 
